## PR Title
Fix RV32E shifts by immediates >= 0x10

## PR Description
Resolves issue #211. Makes shift-by-immediate instructions on the RV32E configuration use the full 5-bit immediate field rather than truncating it to 4 bits, so e.g. `slli` works with shift amounts >= 0x10. The author notes they did not exhaustively test other RV32E instructions but did not find further breakage in cursory testing, and that the change appears not to break Q-register instructions on RV32I (untested).

